<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>KhaozEngine.Catalog.GameTypes</PackageId>
    <Version>$(KhaozEngineVersion)</Version>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <Description>The thirteen game-shaped content types most RPG-shaped worlds re-author from scratch (in Foundation, over KhaozEngine.Catalog): food, equip_profile and its stat lines, store and its shelves, monster_drop, gathering_node, recipe with its inputs and outputs, tool_tier, skill_curve and game_tuning. Each one is a stable type id in the game band, a stable key, an ordered field schema, a row codec and one Register call that supplies all of them plus the type's visibility and chunk slots, so two worlds that author the same facts store them the same way and address them the same way. A GAME DECLARES ITS TIME UNIT through ContentDurationUnit and the four duration fields take the matching name, with identical field order, kinds and codecs under either unit. NINE TYPES SHIP A VALIDATOR: food, equip_stat_line, store, store_shelf, monster_drop, gathering_node, recipe_input, recipe_output and tool_tier, each a nested Validator on its type class emitting the KGT finding codes. The two recipe sides run one rule set through one control flow under two sets of codes, so a report names which side of the recipe is wrong. StoreContentType carries BasisPointDenominator and LargestSafeRateBasisPoints, and its validator reads the engine item type's value field position off the LIVE registry at validation time rather than off a schema built at type load. The remaining two validators and the cross-type sweep are not here yet, and a game passes its own validator to Register for those types until they are. The package owns no vocabulary of its own: a skill, a station, a repeat mode, an npc kind and a monster kind are all raw numbers a game gives meaning to, and there is no enum, no balance number and no roster anywhere in it. Pure .NET, no JSON, no external deps.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The positional *Index constants are internal on purpose: a position is not a consumer's to write
         down. The test project reaches them to pin each one against its schema's own IndexOf, which is what
         makes an off-by-one a failing test rather than a read of the neighbouring field. -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="KhaozEngine.Catalog.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../KhaozEngine.Catalog/KhaozEngine.Catalog.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
